Robert Marenda wrote:
> Now for a question or two. When I find a wand, and I do not have a spare 
> scroll of identify, what are some safe ways to identify it?

Write something in the dust with your fingers and then Engrave with the
wand on the same square.


> I have also been avoiding using fountains and sinks. I fear drinking from 
> fountains because I keep releasing nasties that kill me.

Use fountains only once you can handle the nasties. If you have water
walking or magical breathing and a pick-axe you can turn the fountain
into a pool and use it for #dipping without the chance of getting
nasties. There's usually no point in quaffing from fountains.


> I also have given 
> up on dumping rings down sinks to identify them.

Why? There are no downsides except that you lose the ring. You should
only drop rings that you have a spare of.


